WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.421
Meet Bantera.

2
00:00:01.421 --> 00:00:06.346
A place to turn a little everyday practice into more confident conversations.

3
00:00:06.346 --> 00:00:10.451
Listen to real situations, say your reply out loud, and

4
00:00:10.451 --> 00:00:13.324
make space for speaking in your day.

5
00:00:13.324 --> 00:00:17.429
In this tour, we'll explore short Practice exercises, longer dialogues,

6
00:00:17.429 --> 00:00:21.533
conversations with AI, and simple ways to see your progress.

7
00:00:23.433 --> 00:00:25.165
Start on the Practice page.

8
00:00:25.165 --> 00:00:28.975
Each exercise gives you a short cue and two possible replies.

9
00:00:28.975 --> 00:00:32.439
Tap the speaker to hear the cue, then listen to

10
00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:34.517
either reply if you need to.

11
00:00:34.517 --> 00:00:37.635
Here, someone is asking for a table for two.

12
00:00:37.635 --> 00:00:39.713
Decide which answer fits the conversation.

13
00:00:39.713 --> 00:00:43.177
Then use the microphone to say your chosen reply aloud.

14
00:00:43.177 --> 00:00:47.333
You're practising the sound of the language as well as its meaning.

15
00:00:49.233 --> 00:00:52.713
When your reply is correct, watch the little particles travel

16
00:00:52.713 --> 00:00:55.497
from the recording button to your daily goal.

17
00:00:55.497 --> 00:00:58.281
A rocket gives your progress a little lift.

18
00:00:58.281 --> 00:01:01.761
You can review what was heard and replay your recording,

19
00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:04.196
then move straight to the next exercise.

20
00:01:04.196 --> 00:01:07.676
The success animation celebrates a correct reply, while listening and

21
00:01:07.676 --> 00:01:12.200
speaking still count towards your activity even when an answer needs another try.

22
00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:18.271
Practice difficulty adjusts over time, from A one through C two.

23
00:01:18.271 --> 00:01:20.926
A single answer doesn't decide your level.

24
00:01:20.926 --> 00:01:25.856
Bantera looks at your performance across exercises, so progress comes from repeated practice.

25
00:01:25.856 --> 00:01:28.890
Tap the level button to see your options.

26
00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:32.682
You can revisit a level at or below your current

27
00:01:32.682 --> 00:01:36.474
level, while harder levels remain locked until you reach them.

28
00:01:36.474 --> 00:01:40.267
These are practice levels, rather than a formal language qualification.

29
00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:45.319
Try listening and choosing before revealing a translation.

30
00:01:45.319 --> 00:01:48.865
If you need a little help, tap Show translation.

31
00:01:48.865 --> 00:01:52.806
Bantera explains that using a translation means this exercise won't

32
00:01:52.806 --> 00:01:54.382
affect your level changes.

33
00:01:54.382 --> 00:01:58.323
You can still use it to learn, listen again, and

34
00:01:58.323 --> 00:01:59.899
practise saying the reply.

35
00:01:59.899 --> 00:02:04.233
That keeps help available while making the level adjustment more meaningful.

36
00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:09.693
When you're ready to spend a little longer with a

37
00:02:09.693 --> 00:02:12.540
topic, open the menu and choose Longer dialogues.

38
00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:16.099
Browse the available conversations and find something that interests you.

39
00:02:16.099 --> 00:02:19.659
Everyday situations give the language context, so you can hear

40
00:02:19.659 --> 00:02:21.082
how phrases work together.

41
00:02:21.082 --> 00:02:24.642
The library menu also gives you a way back to

42
00:02:24.642 --> 00:02:27.133
Practice History, Saved Media, and Saved Cues.

43
00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:32.314
Open a dialogue to listen and follow the transcript.

44
00:02:32.314 --> 00:02:35.959
You can return to a useful part, hear it again,

45
00:02:35.959 --> 00:02:38.875
and practise repeating it in your own voice.

46
00:02:38.875 --> 00:02:43.614
Instead of rushing through every sentence, focus on a phrase you'd actually use.

47
00:02:43.614 --> 00:02:47.259
A question in a cafe, an introduction, or a small

48
00:02:47.259 --> 00:02:51.633
moment of everyday conversation can become something you're ready to say yourself.

49
00:02:53.533 --> 00:02:56.815
In Chats, Bantera AI gives you another way to practise.

50
00:02:56.815 --> 00:03:00.096
Open the conversation and use your voice to talk about

51
00:03:00.096 --> 00:03:03.377
a topic, ask a question, or explore a situation you

52
00:03:03.377 --> 00:03:05.018
might meet in daily life.

53
00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:07.315
Listen to the response, then keep going.

54
00:03:07.315 --> 00:03:09.940
You don't need a perfect sentence to start.

55
00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:13.221
The useful part is making speaking a habit and finding

56
00:03:13.221 --> 00:03:14.533
more opportunities to reply.

57
00:03:16.433 --> 00:03:20.056
Chats also brings your conversations with people into one place.

58
00:03:20.056 --> 00:03:23.678
Explore a language group, return to a direct conversation, or

59
00:03:23.678 --> 00:03:25.489
see who's available to talk.

60
00:03:25.489 --> 00:03:29.111
A short exchange can be a reason to use a

61
00:03:29.111 --> 00:03:33.820
new phrase, hear another voice, and learn how someone else expresses an idea.

62
00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:38.167
Keep it friendly, take your time, and let the conversation grow naturally.

63
00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:42.855
Your progress is more than a correct answer.

64
00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:45.991
Listening and speaking both contribute to your daily activity.

65
00:03:45.991 --> 00:03:49.476
Set a goal that feels realistic, and use the progress

66
00:03:49.476 --> 00:03:52.264
circle to see how your day is going.

67
00:03:52.264 --> 00:03:55.748
This sample account is seventy percent of the way there.

68
00:03:55.748 --> 00:03:59.233
In Profile, you can look back at your listening and

69
00:03:59.233 --> 00:04:03.067
speaking activity and see how small sessions add up over time.

70
00:04:04.967 --> 00:04:09.375
And when you reach your full daily goal, Bantera celebrates with you.

71
00:04:09.375 --> 00:04:13.783
The progress circle reaches one hundred percent, and confetti fills the screen.

72
00:04:13.783 --> 00:04:17.457
It is a small moment to recognise the listening and

73
00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:19.294
speaking you have done today.

74
00:04:19.294 --> 00:04:22.600
Enjoy it, then come back tomorrow for another conversation.

75
00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:27.686
You don't have to do everything at once.

76
00:04:27.686 --> 00:04:32.068
Start with one short exercise, listen carefully, and say your reply.

77
00:04:32.068 --> 00:04:37.246
When you have more time, explore a longer dialogue or open a conversation.

78
00:04:37.246 --> 00:04:41.229
Bantera brings those moments together, with a daily goal to

79
00:04:41.229 --> 00:04:42.822
help you keep going.

80
00:04:42.822 --> 00:04:48.000
Visit bantera dot app, and make your next small step a spoken one.
